# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS artefacts
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs (local development artefacts)
*.log

# Claude Code – machine-/user-local permission allowlist
# (settings.json stays versioned for project-wide defaults)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Maintainer-local working state (CCPR dogfooding its own conventions).
# The repo ships docs/ as framework content; these are session artefacts, not
# distribution. Keeping them untracked also keeps tenant identifiers out of
# shipped artefacts (Constitution, Inviolable "No personal or tenant data").
# Decision drafts are extracted into a de-personalised ADR under docs/adr/.
docs/HANDOVER.md
docs/.handover-archive/
docs/decisions/

# Project working state, not framework content: 89 work items about CCPR's own
# defects (560 KB) and 400 KB of persona review notes, which would arrive in an
# installation looking like the user's own state. Framework docs that explain the
# design stay tracked -- and the allowlist named below, not this comment, is what
# says which ones: adr/, logo/, CONSTITUTION.md, NEXT_STEPS_REFERENCE.md,
# PROJECT_PHASES.md.
#
# This paragraph used to end "..., the flat Tier-1 memory files) stay tracked".
# That was never true: `git ls-files docs/memory` has always returned nothing,
# because the rule below ignores docs/memory/ wholesale. Corrected 23.08.2026
# after measuring it rather than reading it.
#
# Tracking those 8 flat files (80 KB) later is NOT a one-line change here. The
# allowlist below serves BOTH sides of the boundary, so "tracked but not shipped"
# is not expressible today: artifact-gate.sh fails a tracked docs/ path that is
# not listed, and install.sh copies exactly what IS listed. Measured 23.08.2026 --
# all 8 files fail the gate's docs-boundary check. Making them tracked-but-local
# means either moving them to a framework home that earns an allowlist entry, or
# splitting the allowlist into two lists, which is an ADR-sized change.
# Since WI-0018, install.sh no longer copies docs/ wholesale: install_docs()
# filters each top-level docs/ child against
# scripts/lib/docs-framework-allowlist.txt and reports what it skipped. This
# ignore rule is therefore no longer the only thing keeping working state out of
# an installation -- but it stays the first line, and it is the one that also
# keeps the state out of a clone. Note the two mechanisms cover different sets:
# the allowlist is per top-level entry and reads the filesystem, so an ignored
# file inside an ALLOWLISTED directory is still installed (see docs/logo/ below).
docs/workitems/
docs/memory/

# Social-preview renders. The tracked logo assets under docs/logo/ (icon SVGs,
# wordmark PNGs) are referenced from the README; these two are not referenced
# from anywhere in the repo -- they exist for a platform's repo-preview slot,
# which is configured in the host's settings rather than from a file.
# They live under assets/, NOT docs/logo/, and that placement is the point:
# docs/logo/ is allowlisted as a whole in scripts/lib/docs-framework-allowlist.txt
# and install_docs() reads the FILESYSTEM rather than the git index, so an ignored
# file in an allowlisted directory is still copied into every installation --
# measured on 21.08.2026, when deleting them from ~/.claude/docs/logo/ was undone
# by the very next `install.sh --update`. assets/ is in no artifact list, so
# nothing here ships. Ignored on top of that, to keep `git status` quiet.
assets/

# WI-0058: volatile generator outputs directly under docs/ (session snapshots,
# gate-preflight notes, quality-scan / cross-check / baseline-prep reports --
# scripts/tests/test_docs_dotfile_gitignore_coverage.py sweeps the shipped
# scripts and commands for the current list). A broad dotfile pattern, not an
# enumeration: this repo tracks no dotfile directly under docs/ today (verified
# via `git ls-files`), and a pattern nobody has to remember to extend is what
# actually keeps pace with a script adding a new report next quarter. A new
# project generated by scripts/project-init.sh gets an enumerated block instead
# -- a user's docs/ may deliberately track a dotfile this repo does not.
docs/.*
